Package: EHML
Title: Easy Hyperparameter Optimization for Machine Learning
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Sicong", "Zheng",
           email = "zhengsicong020655@163.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: EHML (Easy Hyperparameter Optimization for Machine Learning)
    is a user-friendly framework for machine learning model development.
    The package integrates feature selection, hyperparameter optimization,
    model construction, performance evaluation, and applicability assessment.
    It supports multiple machine learning algorithms and provides automated
    recommendations based on sample size, outcome balance, and predictor
    dimensions. EHML is designed to facilitate reproducible and interpretable
    machine learning analyses in biomedical and clinical research.
    For reproducibility, 'plsRglm' version 1.5.1 and 'xgboost' version
    1.5.2.1 are recommended. Most algorithms are implemented in R,
    whereas the neural network module requires a separately installed
    Python environment with compatible versions of 'Keras' and
    'TensorFlow'. Users should configure Python before running the
    neural network module.
